row\",\"children\":\"Commercials\"}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"engagement\",\"className\":\"sv-h2\",\"children\":\"Shape, timeline and scoping\"}],null]}],[\"$\",\"dl\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-defs\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-def\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"dt\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-def__term\",\"children\":\"Timeline\"}],[\"$\",\"dd\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-def__desc\",\"children\":\"4–8 months to first production release for a typical business system.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-def\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"dt\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-def__term\",\"children\":\"Team shape\"}],[\"$\",\"dd\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-def__desc\",\"children\":\"A tech lead, two to five engineers, a designer, and a part-time delivery lead. A security engineer at the design and hardening gates.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-def\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"dt\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-def__term\",\"children\":\"Engagement\"}],[\"$\",\"dd\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-def__desc\",\"children\":\"Fixed-scope phases with a time-and-materials build, or a dedicated squad on a quarterly commitment.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-def\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"dt\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-def__term\",\"children\":\"Scoping\"}],[\"$\",\"dd\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-def__desc\",\"children\":[\"A named engineer replies within one business day. Scoping call within three.\",\" \",[\"$\",\"$Le\",null,{\"className\":\"u-link\",\"href\":\"/services/engagement-models\",\"children\":\"How the four engagement models differ\"}],\".\"]}]]}]]}]]}]}]]\n37:[[\"$\",\"style\",null,{\"href\":\"envenox-section\",\"precedence\":\"default\",\"children\":\"\\n.sec {\\n  position: relative;\\n  background-color: var(--bg);\\n  color: var(--fg);\\n}\\n/* Grain sits at z-index 1 with pointer-events none; content rides above it. */\\n.sec > .u-container,\\n.sec > .sec__bleed { position: relative; z-index: 2; }\\n\"}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"sec theme-light transition-theme u-section-tight\",\"data-theme-section\":\"light\",\"style\":\"$undefined\",\"aria-labelledby\":\"topics\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"u-container\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-head\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-head__rule\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"u-eyebrow sv-head__eyebrow\",\"children\":\"Explainers\"}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"topics\",\"className\":\"sv-h2\",\"children\":\"Questions about Custom Software\"}],null]}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-links\",\"aria-label\":\"Questions buyers ask about this service\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"/services/custom-software/fixed-price-or-time-and-materialsFixed price or time and materials?\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Le\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-links__a\",\"href\":\"/services/custom-software/fixed-price-or-time-and-materials\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-links__label\",\"children\":[\"Fixed price or time and materials?\",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-links__blurb\",\"children\":\"We want a fixed price. Why are you resisting?\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-links__arrow\",\"width\":\"16\",\"height\":\"16\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":\"1.75\",\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"focusable\":\"false\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"d\":\"M5 12h14\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"d\":\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\"}]]}]]}]}]]}]]}]}]]\n38:[[\"$\",\"style\",null,{\"href\":\"envenox-section\",\"precedence\":\"default\",\"children\":\"\\n.sec {\\n  position: relative;\\n  background-color: var(--bg);\\n  color: var(--fg);\\n}\\n/* Grain sits at z-index 1 with pointer-events none; content rides above it. */\\n.sec > .u-container,\\n.sec > .sec__bleed { position: relative; z-index: 2; }\\n\"}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"sec theme-light transition-theme u-section\",\"data-theme-section\":\"light\",\"style\":\"$undefined\",\"aria-labelledby\":\"faq\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"u-container\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-head\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-head__rule\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"u-eyebrow sv-head__eyebrow\",\"children\":\"Questions\"}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"faq\",\"className\":\"sv-h2\",\"children\":\"Frequently asked\"}],null]}],[\"$\",\"$L82\",null,{\"items\":[{\"q\":\"Fixed price or time and materials?\",\"a\":\"Discovery is fixed price, because it is a bounded piece of work with a defined output. The build is time and materials against a prioritised backlog with a cap and a monthly review. A fixed price for a build you have not designed yet is priced for the worst case and spent defending the scope boundary.\"},{\"q\":\"Who owns the code?\",\"a\":\"You do, from the first commit, in your repository. No escrow arrangement, no licence-back, no runtime dependency on us. If you want to take it in-house after discovery, the discovery output is designed to be usable by another firm.\"},{\"q\":\"Can you work with our existing team?\",\"a\":\"Routinely, and it is usually the better arrangement. We pair, we review each other’s pull requests, and we aim to leave your engineers more capable than we found them. We will not run a parallel team that throws work over a wall.\"},{\"q\":\"What if requirements change?\",\"a\":\"They will. The backlog is prioritised and reviewed every sprint, the cap is reviewed monthly, and a change that invalidates an architectural decision gets a new decision record rather than a quiet workaround. What we will not do is absorb scope silently and then explain the overrun at the end.\"},{\"q\":\"How do you handle accessibility?\",\"a\":\"WCAG 2.2 AA is the baseline, designed in rather than audited on. Keyboard operation, focus management, announced errors and reduced-motion paths are acceptance criteria on each story, and an axe-core run is a CI gate. Retrofitting accessibility after launch costs several times what building it in does.\"},{\"q\":\"Do you build mobile?\",\"a\":\"Yes — React Native where a shared codebase is right, native Swift or Kotlin where the application is genuinely platform-specific. We will tell you which during discovery and explain the trade-off rather than defaulting to whichever we prefer.\"},{\"q\":\"What happens after launch?\",\"a\":\"Whichever was planned in discovery. Either a documented handover with paired work and a recorded tour, or a support agreement with a response SLA and a named engineer. The failure mode is deciding this in the last week, which is why it is a discovery output.\"},{\"q\":\"Will your security practice test what you build?\",\"a\":\"Yes, and the report comes to you unedited. A separate lead tester who did not write the code signs it. If you would rather a third party tested it, we will support that and share the threat model with them.\"}],\"headingLevel\":3}]]}]}]]\n83:{\"id\":\"403c44504416ed33d4af4350092b655f174641e336\",\"bound\":null}\n39:[[\"$\",\"style\",null,{\"href\":\"envenox-section\",\"precedence\":\"default\",\"children\":\"\\n.sec {\\n  position: relative;\\n  background-color: var(--bg);\\n  color: var(--fg);\\n}\\n/* Grain sits at z-index 1 with pointer-events none; content rides above it. */\\n.sec > .u-container,\\n.sec > .sec__bleed { position: relative; z-index: 2; }\\n\"}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"sec theme-light transition-theme u-section grain\",\"data-theme-section\":\"light\",\"style\":\"$undefined\",\"aria-labelledby\":\"enquiry-h2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"u-container\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-rail\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-rail__aside\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"u-eyebrow\",\"children\":\"Get started\"}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"enquiry-h2\",\"className\":\"sv-h2\",\"style\":{\"marginTop\":\"var(--s3)\"},\"children\":\"Book a 60-minute scoping call\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-lede\",\"children\":\"A technical conversation with the person who would lead the work — not a qualification script, not a discovery deck. You come away with a written scope, the exclusions stated in the body rather than in an appendix, and a day count that we have not padded.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-note\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":16,\"height\":16,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":1.75,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-users\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"style\":{\"display\":\"inline-block\",\"verticalAlign\":\"-3px\",\"marginRight\":\"var(--s2)\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",\"1yyitq\",{\"d\":\"M16 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"16gr8j\",{\"d\":\"M16 3.128a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.744\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"kshegd\",{\"d\":\"M22 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87\"}],[\"$\",\"circle\",\"nufk8\",{\"cx\":\"9\",\"cy\":\"7\",\"r\":\"4\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],\"A tech lead, two to five engineers, a designer, and a part-time delivery lead. A security engineer at the design and hardening gates.\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-rail__body\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"form\",null,{\"action\":\"$h83\",\"className\":\"sv-form\",\"id\":\"enquiry-form\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"input\",null,{\"type\":\"hidden\",\"name\":\"returnTo\",\"value\":\"/services/custom-software\"}],[[\"$\",\"div\",\"enquiry-incomplete\",{\"id\":\"enquiry-incomplete\",\"className\":\"sv-form__error\",\"role\":\"alert\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Some required fields came through empty. They are marked below — fill them in and send again.\"}]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"enquiry-email\",{\"id\":\"enquiry-email\",\"className\":\"sv-form__error\",\"role\":\"alert\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"That email address did not look complete. Check it and send again.\"}]}]],[[\"$\",\"div\",\"name\",{\"className\":\"sv-field\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"label\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-label\",\"htmlFor\":\"enq-name\",\"children\":[\"Your name\",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-req\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":\"*\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"input\",null,{\"id\":\"enq-name\",\"name\":\"name\",\"className\":\"sv-input\",\"type\":\"text\",\"required\":true,\"autoComplete\":\"name\",\"aria-describedby\":\"$undefined\"}],null]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"email\",{\"className\":\"sv-field\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"label\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-label\",\"htmlFor\":\"enq-email\",\"children\":[\"Business email\",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-req\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":\"*\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"input\",null,{\"id\":\"enq-email\",\"name\":\"email\",\"className\":\"sv-input\",\"type\":\"email\",\"required\":true,\"autoComplete\":\"email\",\"aria-describedby\":\"enq-email-help\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-help\",\"id\":\"enq-email-help\",\"children\":\"We reply from a person, not a no-reply address.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"company\",{\"className\":\"sv-field\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"label\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-label\",\"htmlFor\":\"enq-company\",\"children\":[\"Company\",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-req\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":\"*\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"input\",null,{\"id\":\"enq-company\",\"name\":\"company\",\"className\":\"sv-input\",\"type\":\"text\",\"required\":true,\"autoComplete\":\"organization\",\"aria-describedby\":\"$undefined\"}],null]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"country\",{\"className\":\"sv-field\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"label\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-label\",\"htmlFor\":\"enq-country\",\"children\":[\"Country\",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-req\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":\"*\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"input\",null,{\"id\":\"enq-country\",\"name\":\"country\",\"className\":\"sv-input\",\"type\":\"text\",\"required\":true,\"autoComplete\":\"country-name\",\"aria-describedby\":\"enq-country-help\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-help\",\"id\":\"enq-country-help\",\"children\":\"Relevant for data residency and time zone.\"}]]}],\"$L84\",\"$L85\",\"$L86\"],\"$L87\",\"$L88\"]}]}]]}]}]}]]\n89:Tdb3,\n.btn {\n  --btn-bg: transparent;\n  --btn-bg-hover: transparent;\n  --btn-fg: var(--fg);\n  --btn-border: transparent;\n  --btn-border-hover: transparent;\n\n  display: inline-flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n  gap: var(--s2);\n  border: 1px solid var(--btn-border);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  background-color: var(--btn-bg);\n  color: var(--btn-fg);\n  font-family: var(--font-inter-tight), var(--font-inter), ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;\n  font-weight: 500;\n  letter-spacing: -0.01em;\n  line-height: 1;\n  text-align: center;\n  text-decoration: none;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  /* ONLY colour transitions. A transform here would break the house rule. */\n  transition:\n    background-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out),\n    border-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out),\n    color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.btn:hover {\n  background-color: var(--btn-bg-hover);\n  border-color: var(--btn-border-hover);\n  /* Falls back to the resting label colour, so no existing variant changes.\n     A variant whose hover fill moves far in lightness needs to move its label\n     too, or the hover state quietly fails contrast while the resting state\n     passes — which is the kind of thing an audit on static screenshots misses. */\n  color: var(--btn-fg-hover, var(--btn-fg));\n}\n.btn[aria-disabled='true'],\n.btn:disabled {\n  opacity: 0.45;\n  cursor: not-allowed;\n}\n.btn[aria-disabled='true']:hover,\n.btn:disabled:hover {\n  background-color: var(--btn-bg);\n  border-color: var(--btn-border);\n}\n\n/* ---- sizes. md and lg clear the 44x44 touch target. ---- */\n.btn--sm { min-height: 32px; padding-inline: var(--s3); font-size: var(--text-sm); }\n.btn--md { min-height: 44px; min-width: 44px; padding-inline: var(--s4); font-size: var(--text-sm); }\n.btn--lg { min-height: 52px; min-width: 52px; padding-inline: var(--s6); font-size: var(--text-base); }\n\n.btn--full { width: 100%; }\n\n/* ---- variants ---- */\n.btn--primary {\n  --btn-bg: var(--accent);\n  --btn-fg: var(--accent-fg);\n  --btn-bg-hover: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 82%, var(--fg) 18%);\n  --btn-border: var(--accent);\n  --btn-border-hover: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 82%, var(--fg) 18%);\n}\n.theme-light .btn--primary {\n  /* On paper, --accent is the DARK copper (#A04F1A) because it has to pass\n     4.5:1 as link TEXT. As a large filled surface that same value reads muddy\n     brown, which is not what the brand is. A fill has a different contrast\n     problem from text: the requirement is on the LABEL against the fill, and\n     ink on vibrant copper measures 6.9:1 — comfortably clear. So the fill gets\n     the real brand copper and the label goes dark. Links and the focus ring\n     keep --accent and stay legible. */\n  --btn-bg: var(--accent-500);\n  --btn-fg: var(--ink-900);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--accent-600);\n  --btn-fg-hover: var(--paper-50);\n  --btn-border: var(--accent-500);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--accent-600);\n}\n.btn--secondary {\n  --btn-fg: var(--fg);\n  --btn-border: var(--border-strong);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--surface);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--fg);\n}\n.btn--ghost {\n  --btn-fg: var(--muted-strong);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--surface);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--border);\n}\n.btn--ghost:hover { color: var(--fg); }\n.btn--danger-quiet {\n  --btn-fg: var(--muted-strong);\n  --btn-border: var(--border-strong);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--surface);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--muted-strong);\n}\n.btn--danger-quiet:hover { color: var(--fg); }\n\n.btn__icon { display: inline-flex; flex: none; }\n3a:[[\"$\",\"style\",null,{\"href\":\"envenox-section\",\"precedence\":\"default\",\"children\":\"\\n.sec {\\n  position: relative;\\n  background-color: var(--bg);\\n  color: var(--fg);\\n}\\n/* Grain sits at z-index 1 with pointer-events none; content rides above it. */\\n.sec > .u-container,\\n.sec > .sec__bleed { position: relative; z-index: 2; }\\n\"}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"sec theme-light transition-theme u-section-tight\",\"data-theme-section\":\"light\",\"style\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"u-container\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-cta-band\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-h2\",\"children\":\"Systems built to survive an audit, a breach attempt and a handover.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-lede\",\"children\":\"Fixed-scope phases with a time-and-materials build, or a dedicated squad on a quarterly commitment.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-cta-band__actions\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"style\",null,{\"href\":\"envenox-button\",\"precedence\":\"default\",\"children\":\"$89\"}],\"$L8a\"],\"$L8b\"]}]]}]}]}]]\n3d:[\"$\",\"$Le\",null,{\"href\":\"/contact\",\"className\":\"btn btn--primary btn--lg\",\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Start a conversation\"}],null]}]\n8c:Tdb3,\n.btn {\n  --btn-bg: transparent;\n  --btn-bg-hover: transparent;\n  --btn-fg: var(--fg);\n  --btn-border: transparent;\n  --btn-border-hover: transparent;\n\n  display: inline-flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n  gap: var(--s2);\n  border: 1px solid var(--btn-border);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  background-color: var(--btn-bg);\n  color: var(--btn-fg);\n  font-family: var(--font-inter-tight), var(--font-inter), ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;\n  font-weight: 500;\n  letter-spacing: -0.01em;\n  line-h